 3. **Release notes** — experimental flags and breaking changes.
 
 For API request fields (`networkPolicy`, volumes, etc.), see the OpenAPI specs under [`specs/`](../specs/) and the [Server README](README.md).
+
+## BBX G7 Server-only opt-in patch
+
+`[kubernetes].batchsandbox_informer_enabled` defaults to `true`. Set it to
+`false` only for the fixed non-pooled BatchSandbox profile to disable Server
+read/creation-wait informers for that GVR. Existing namespace/selector checks,
+read limits and creation polling remain; direct GET/LIST use a (10, 30) second
+connect/read budget. Controller, ingress and explicit snapshot/template
+reactors are unchanged. This is not an official 1.2.0 configuration option.
+
+`[tenants].cache_max_entries` defaults to `0` (legacy). A positive bound opts
+HTTP tenants into lazy expiry after TTL plus max-stale and LRU eviction.
+Active keys resolve again through the authoritative endpoint after eviction.
+The cache is a bounded hint set, never the active-Task inventory. Background
+namespace discovery still needs the existing label-scoped cluster LIST RBAC.
+401, provider failures and max-stale policy are not relaxed. No timer or new
+cache service is introduced. The flag is process-wide; do not switch active
+legacy task bindings without a coordinated deployment boundary.
